<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71474" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεινήϊον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεῖνος</span>) only found in 
			Ion.
		 and 
			Ep.
		 form, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>host's
			gift</i> to a guest, in full 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρα ξεινήϊα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.273
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντὶ ποδὸς ξεινήϊον,</span>
			ironically, <i><span class="en">
				22.290
			</span></i> ; also, <i>provision made for a guest,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεινήϊα πολλὰ φαγόντε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.33
				</span></i>
			 : more generally, <i>gifts of (guest-) friendship,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλοισι πόρον ξεινήϊα καλά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.218
				</span></i>
			.</div>
